## Terms of Service Warning

**Client modifications violate Discord's Terms of Service.**

> Don't use the services to do harm to Discord. Among other things, this includes...
> using any unauthorized software designed to modify the services...
> — [Discord Terms of Service](https://discord.com/terms)

Vencord is a Discord client mod. Plugins that run inside Vencord modify the
Discord client at runtime, which technically violates Discord's ToS.

However, Discord is generally indifferent to client mods in practice. There are
no known cases of users getting banned for using Vencord with non-abusive
plugins. **Do not** write plugins that:
- Automate sending messages (self-botting) — this **does** get accounts banned
- Scrape or exfiltrate data to external servers
- Implement abusive behavior (mass-mention, spam, raid tools)

All built-in Vencord plugins are considered safe. If your account is important
to you, consider the risk before using any client mod.

## Getting Started

### Prerequisites

- [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/) >= 20
- [pnpm](https://pnpm.io/) >= 9
- A local [Vencord](https://github.com/Vendicated/Vencord) checkout

### Install

```bash
pnpm install
```

### Build

```bash
pnpm run build
```

This compiles the TypeScript sources into the `dist/` directory.

### Test

```bash
pnpm test
```

Runs unit tests with Vitest. Tests mock Vencord's internal modules to validate
the plugin definition without requiring a full Vencord checkout.

### Lint & Typecheck

```bash
pnpm run lint
pnpm run typecheck
```

## Linking to Vencord

To test your plugin inside Vencord, link it into your Vencord checkout:

```bash
pnpm run link:vencord
```

This creates a symlink from `<vencord>/src/userplugins/{{ package_name }}` to
this project's `src/` directory. After linking, rebuild Vencord:

```bash
cd ~/p/gh/Vendicated/Vencord
pnpm build
```

Then launch Discord with Vencord loaded. Your plugin will appear in the
Vencord settings under the Plugins tab.

To override the Vencord checkout path:

```bash
VENCORD_REPO_PATH=~/path/to/Vencord pnpm run link:vencord
```

## Project Structure

```text
.
├─ src/
│  ├─ index.ts          # Plugin entry point (definePlugin)
│  ├─ settings.ts       # Plugin settings (definePluginSettings)
│  └─ native.ts         # Node.js native code (desktop only, optional)
├─ __tests__/
│  └─ plugin.test.mts   # Unit tests
├─ scripts/
│  └─ link-vencord.sh   # Symlink plugin into Vencord checkout
├─ package.json
├─ tsconfig.json
├─ vitest.config.mts
└─ project.json         # Nx project targets
```

## Plugin API

This plugin uses the Vencord plugin API. Key concepts:

- **`definePlugin`** — The main function that registers your plugin with Vencord
- **`patches`** — Webpack module patches that modify Discord's bundled code
- **`commands`** — Slash commands registered by your plugin
- **`settings`** — User-configurable options shown in the Vencord settings UI
- **`start()` / `stop()`** — Lifecycle hooks called when the plugin is enabled/disabled
- **`native.ts`** — Node.js-only code (desktop client), for file system or process access

See the [Vencord plugin documentation](https://docs.vencord.dev/plugins/) for
detailed API reference.

## Scripts

| Script | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| `pnpm run build` | Compile TypeScript to `dist/` |
| `pnpm run dev` | Watch-mode TypeScript compilation |
| `pnpm test` | Run unit tests with Vitest |
| `pnpm run lint` | Lint source files with ESLint |
| `pnpm run typecheck` | Type-check without emitting |
| `pnpm run format` | Format code with Prettier |
| `pnpm run link:vencord` | Symlink plugin into local Vencord checkout |
| `pnpm run clean` | Remove build artifacts |

